PRETABLE -- #529 kill table 2 (TARGETED), written BEFORE the table (mtime is the order proof)
Instrument: regress/crime_width_probe.py as repaired after pass 2 -- 71 rows (42 -> 50 row() call sites; 59 -> 71
emitted), frozen by the driver as crime_width_probe.table2.py.  First measurement (L1): build/ 71/71 CONTROL=OK
(../probe_first2_fix.out, after propagating the comment-only source edit to all four trees: build/ build-asan/
/tmp/gxsec-build p1=CLEAN p2=FRESH, est/ p1=CLEAN p2=N/A).  Baseline = the #529 working set (the comment edit
included), rebuilt in the clone.

SUPERSET WARRANT for targeting: every table-1 session's command sequence is unchanged; every table-1 row is present
with the same oracle or a STRICTER one (the `said' pattern now includes `(once) ]'); session() gained only the <RUN>
command and a SIGKILL for a session that never reached EOF (a clean session is unaffected).  So every table-1 kill
stands; BASE is re-measured for a false red.  Table-1's mutants are NOT re-run.

WHAT CHANGED IN THE DETECTOR, and the finding that bought each row (pass 2, panel_20260913_022247 + Opus)
  sb/sh rev pc      the REV-store cell (codex, grok, glm; Opus a_revw measured 40/40)
  imask/istat pre, lb, sb, ctl     the reassert at INTMASK/INTSTAT (minimax named it; Opus MEASURED it)
  time lb/sb (+ ctl)               the TIME update (codex, kimi; Opus MEASURED it)
  lb/lh/sb/sh/hi nodflt, dflt ctl  address-keyed fall-through into the default arm (grok, minimax; Opus a_lo10 trace)
  sb keeps, sh keeps               a refused store that lands (codex)
  sb08 run                         `sb08 msg' was green under exit0 (codex)
  top8/top4 rows at +0x278         accept cells pinned only at CRIME_DOG (kimi CLI; Opus x_mc4/x_mc8 measured 40/40)
  hi said/nodflt/surv at +0x27f    address-keyed announce (kimi CLI; Opus l_addrmask measured 40/40)
  said pattern + `(once) ]'        the marker unmeasured (codex; Opus l_noonce measured 40/40)
  free said, free v0               fatal() -> debug() (codex)

CHANNEL -- per mutant, the rows PREDICTED to red (anything else reddening is a finding about the prediction)
  base      none (71/71)
  revwrite  sb rev pc, sh rev pc
  addrrc    lb/lh/sb/sh nodflt, hi nodflt, imask lb, imask sb, istat lb, istat sb, time lb, time sb
  mmreads   lb nodflt, lh nodflt, imask lb, imask sb (IP2 is sticky), istat lb, istat sb, time lb
  fdebug    free said                                             (stepped said rows stay green: debug prints while
                                                                   stepping -- that is why the free row exists)
  wstore    sb keeps, sh keeps, imask ctl (the refused sb +0x18 stores 0 into INTMASK, so the control cannot reassert)
  acc8dog   top8 st+ld, top4 rhi, top4 rlo, top4 w, imask ctl, istat ctl, time lb ctl, time sb ctl
  acc4low   top4 rhi, top4 rlo, top4 w
  annlow    hi said
  only1r    lb nodflt, lb rev pc, imask lb, imask sb, istat lb, istat sb, time lb
  only2r    lh nodflt, lh rev pc
  only1w    sb nodflt, sb08 msg, sb rev pc, imask sb, istat sb, time sb, hi nodflt
  only2w    sh nodflt, sh08 pc, sh08 run, sh rev pc
  a_lo10    sb nodflt, sh nodflt, hi nodflt, imask lb, imask sb, istat lb, istat sb, time lb, time sb
  a_istat   istat lb, istat sb
  timeft    time lb, time sb
  imaskft   imask lb, imask sb
  l_noonce  lb/lh/sb/sh said, hi said, free said
  l_addrmask hi said
  x_mc4     top4 rhi, top4 rlo, top4 w
  x_mc8     top8 st+ld, top4 rhi, top4 rlo, top4 w
  PREDICTED SURVIVORS (71/71), disclosed in the header:
  dogft     `!= CRIME_DOG' -- the DOG arm is `break;'                    EQUIVALENT
  ctlrdft   CONTROL reads fall in -- the arm acts only on MEM_WRITE       EQUIVALENT (no row reads +0x08 narrow)
  acc8mid   `len == 8 && relative_addr != 0x100' -- an interior slot     DISCLOSED coverage debt (header bullet)

ON THE TABLE-1 INSTRUMENT (40 rows), to MEASURE the seats' claimed escapes not already measured by Opus:
  addrrc, mmreads, fdebug, wstore, acc8dog, acc4low, annlow -- each PREDICTED 40/40 (escape)

